{"id": "EUVD-2026-98711", "enisaUuid": "98f498f5-6d40-3bf7-834f-6af5f6783863", "description": "FreeRDP 3.11.0 before 3.32.0 does not validate that AVC444 and AVC444v2 region widths are even before YUV444 conversion, so an odd width reaches an assertion and aborts the client. A malicious or compromised RDP server can terminate a connected FreeRDP client after RDPGFX AVC444 negotiation by sending an in-bounds region rectangle with an odd width.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T13:27:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:08:53", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-97pf-pwp3-2wrv", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.11.0-before-3.32.0-reachable-assertion-via-avc444-odd-region-width"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vqwq-3725-m59m", "CVE-2026-109946"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3b835624-91e7-3b68-8fc3-87ad037c427e", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.11.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ff86ddae-6440-3766-a13e-1cccbbd74b6e", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}